{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|LL.}} ''[[prisma]]'', from {{grc}} [[πρίσμα]] ''prisma'' "something sawed", from [[πρίζειν]] ''prizein'' "to saw".

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-us-prism.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|geometry}} A [[polyhedron]] with [[parallel]] ends of the same size and shape, the other faces being [[parallelogram]]-shaped sides.
# A transparent block in the shape of a prism (typically with triangular ends), used to split or reflect light.
# A crystal in which the faces are parallel to the [[vertical]] [[axis]].

